Relevant columns and their potential usage  
`Year`: needed to pick the two comparison years ( 2012‑01‑01  and 2017‑01‑01).  
`GeoName`: county (or region) name; filter on rows whose value ends with “MA”.  
`Earnings_per_job_avg`: the metric whose increase we want to measure (average earnings per job, in dollars).  

Typical filter conditions  
• `WHERE Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')`  
• `WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'`  (or, safer, `LOWER(GeoName) LIKE '%, ma'`)  

Below are ten exploratory → analytical queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to the final difference‑calculation.  
Replace `project.dataset.table` with the actual identifier  
`bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few Massachusetts rows to understand the shape of the data.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct Massachusetts GeoNames that have data in the table.
SELECT DISTINCT GeoName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show average‐earnings‐per‐job values for 2012 only (MA counties).
SELECT GeoName,
       Earnings_per_job_avg
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE Year = DATE '2012-01-01'
  AND GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Show average‐earnings‐per‐job values for 2017 only (MA counties).
SELECT GeoName,
       Earnings_per_job_avg
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE Year = DATE '2017-01-01'
  AND GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Use a self‑join to place 2012 and 2017 values on the same row.
SELECT a.GeoName,
       a.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_2012,
       b.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS b
  ON a.GeoName = b.GeoName
WHERE a.Year = DATE '2012-01-01'
  AND b.Year = DATE '2017-01-01'
  AND a.GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Same self‑join, but also calculate the increase.
SELECT a.GeoName,
       a.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_2012,
       b.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_2017,
       b.Earnings_per_job_avg - a.Earnings_per_job_avg AS earnings_increase
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips` AS b
  ON a.GeoName = b.GeoName
WHERE a.Year = DATE '2012-01-01'
  AND b.Year = DATE '2017-01-01'
  AND a.GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Achieve the same goal with conditional aggregation instead of a join.
SELECT
  GeoName,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END)
    - MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_increase
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
  AND GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
GROUP BY GeoName
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Only show counties where earnings actually increased; order by size.
SELECT
  GeoName,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END)
    - MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_increase
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
  AND GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
GROUP BY GeoName
HAVING earnings_increase > 0
ORDER BY earnings_increase DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Use a window function to grab 2012 & 2017 values then pivot.
WITH ma AS (
  SELECT
    GeoName,
    Year,
    Earnings_per_job_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
  WHERE Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
    AND GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
)
SELECT DISTINCT
  GeoName,
  FIRST_VALUE(Earnings_per_job_avg) OVER (PARTITION BY GeoName ORDER BY Year) AS earnings_2012,
  LAST_VALUE(Earnings_per_job_avg)  OVER (PARTITION BY GeoName ORDER BY Year
           ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING) AS earnings_2017,
  LAST_VALUE(Earnings_per_job_avg)  OVER (PARTITION BY GeoName ORDER BY Year
           ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING)
  - FIRST_VALUE(Earnings_per_job_avg) OVER (PARTITION BY GeoName ORDER BY Year) AS earnings_increase
FROM ma
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description (FINAL): Produce the increase in average earnings per job
-- for every Massachusetts county, sorted from largest to smallest.
SELECT
  GeoName,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2012,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_2017,
  MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2017-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END)
    - MAX(CASE WHEN Year = DATE '2012-01-01' THEN Earnings_per_job_avg END) AS earnings_increase
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_bea_cainc30.fips`
WHERE Year IN (DATE '2012-01-01', DATE '2017-01-01')
  AND GeoName LIKE '%, MA'
GROUP BY GeoName
ORDER BY earnings_increase DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
